## output
probe: integers in order are deduplicated
[ 1 ::  2 ::  3 :: ]
probe: a pair out of order is returned untouched — it is never searched again
[ 2 ::  1 :: ]
probe: strings in order are deduplicated
[ a ::  b :: ]
probe: strings out of order are not refused
[ b ::  a :: ]
probe: and the search over them skips — the second c goes, the second a stays
[ c ::  b ::  a ::  a :: ]
probe: a CALL carries its name as text, so two of them are one
[ F(true) ::  F(false) :: ]
probe: lists are equal only by identity, so both are kept
[ [ 1 :: ] ::  [ 1 :: ] :: ]
probe: an integer and a string do not collide
[ 1 ::  a :: ]
probe: unique. reads the workbench and answers there
